  "rationale": "The retained agenda notice (retained-agenda), posted by City Secretary Alex Busken on March 20, 2020, explicitly convenes 'a meeting of the Environmental Task Force of the City of Arlington, Texas' for March 24, 2020 at 11:00 a.m., held by telephone under COVID-19 social distancing, and the attached agenda is headed 'ARLINGTON ENVIRONMENTAL TASK FORCE, CITY OF ARLINGTON.' The provider player page (provider-player) labels the same Granicus clip_id 3424 as an 'Environmental Task Force Meeting,' matching the recording date. This establishes the convened body as the Arlington Environmental Task Force, distinct from any venue, topic, or subscription grouping. The existing feed slug 'arlington-tx-environmental-task-force' ('Verified 2020 Arlington Environmental Task Force proceedings') directly matches this 2020 Task Force proceeding, so the recording is assigned there. The general 'arlington-tx' feed is scoped by its own description to City Council and Planning & Zoning meetings only, so it is not an appropriate grouping for this body. The notice names no other convening body or joint participant (all members attend by telephone), so no additional body assignments are proven. Publication rules allow a single proven body's recording to be assigned to its configured feed; no archive/exclusion rule applies because this is a regular public meeting, not a ceremony, film, or forum."
